  "interpretation": "Replicated Generalizability-Theory (G-Theory) design across 5 conceptual frameworks with 3 independently authored, semantically equivalent probe realizations per framework (15 banks total, N=1,800 cell observations; N=14,400 item observations) rigorously separates true article x framework interaction from probe wording sensitivity and residual noise. Under the cell-mean model: Genuine Article x Framework interaction accounts for 37.32% of variance (95% CI: [31.64%, 42.92%]), Framework main effects account for 16.66% (95% CI: [11.25%, 22.20%]), Probe wording variation within framework accounts for 15.33%, Article x wording sensitivity accounts for 30.70%, and stable article-intrinsic effects account for 0.00% (95% CI: [0.00%, 1.29%]). Crucially, genuine article x framework interaction remains decisive (F=4.65, p < 1e-16) even after wording variation and article-by-wording sensitivity are formally isolated. Relative G-coefficient is 0.0000 and dependability Phi is 0.0000."
